 "note": "R142 - PS3 same-size / same-format board-raster writer inputs (after-receipt-5 research package 2, 28 Sep 2026). Research probe, NOT a\nStudio writer and not a write authorisation. Read-only on the installs; mutations only on package-owned disposable copies.\n  A  `board_edges_checked`: the R127f material -> raster edge with every bound the coordinator asked for (predecessor exists, is 0xEF0001,\n     lies inside the header region, reaches +260; slot word names an in-range 0x20003 descriptor of >= 0x38 B inside the header region;\n     signature 83f1 / 83f2 / 83f3 on both format words; descriptor u32 @0 names an in-range 0x10030 data entry whose span lies in the data\n     region, overlaps no other data entry and is owned by no other descriptor; entry size == the plain chain). Replaces r137b.board_edges,\n     which read +256 without a block-length check.\n  B  synthetic malformed packages (built in memory): one valid baseline and one variant per refusal; the r137b helper is run on the\n     short-block variant to show the old read past the block.\n  C  census on every PS3 venue package: loose NHL 14 / 15 / Legacy, archive-only NHL 11 / 12 / 13 (chunkzip members unwrapped in memory):\n     edge outcomes, board rasters per format / level count, materials per raster, refusals.\n  D  full-chain round trips on disposable copies (one sample per format and topology): every level replaced by format-valid solid blocks\n     (a distinct colour / alpha per level), then: bytes outside the entry unchanged, 0 .. hdr_size unchanged, every checked edge unchanged,\n     each level decoded by Pillow's BCn decoder (independent of the writer) = its level colour, the stock entry also decodes level by\n     level; restore by byte copy -> SHA-256 of the source. Container: archive member unwrapped == loose original (pairs); Python zlib-9\n     native chunkzip framing (mirror of tdb-archive-codec compress_chunkzip_native) of the unmodified package == the stock member?;\n     re-wrap of the mutated package decodes back exactly; stored member length stock vs new.\nUsage: python r142_ps3_board_raster_writer.py <out.json> <scratch dir>\n",
